cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Gazebo Gymnasium: Gazebo Harmonic robots as Gymnasium reinforcement-learning environments"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wendland
    given-names: Lucas
    email: lwendlan@umd.edu
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-20"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/CursedRock17/gazebo_gymnasium"
abstract: >-
  Gazebo Gymnasium exposes robots simulated in Gazebo Harmonic as standard
  Farama Gymnasium environments trainable with Stable-Baselines3. A single
  AgentSpec dataclass describes one agent — its model, observation, action,
  reward, and termination — and the framework runs N copies of it in one
  Gazebo world as a vectorized environment, with the simulator optionally
  hosted inside the training process for headless, unthrottled rollouts.
  It ships eight environments, including MuJoCo-equivalent locomotion tasks
  and a camera-based line follower that learns from pixels.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - robotics
  - Gazebo
  - Gymnasium
  - ROS 2
  - simulation
  - sim-to-real
